1
00:04:05,714 --> 00:04:11,714
The Lullaby is a horror film directed by Darrell James Roodt.

2
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:17,428
Returning to her home town, overwhelmed by the birth of her firstborn,
nineteen-year-old Chloe van Heerden tries to come to terms with motherhood.

3
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:23,142
Despite the support from her own mother, Chloe struggles with
the demands of caring for a newborn child.

4
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:28,857
The incessant crying of her baby, the growing sense of guilt
and paranoia send her into a dark depression.

5
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:34,571
With a heightened urge to protect her son, she sees danger everywhere.

6
00:24:34,285 --> 00:24:40,285
Chloe van Heerden, played by Reine Swart.

7
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Adam Hess, played by Deanre Reiners.

8
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:51,714
Ruby van Heerden, played by Thandi Puren.

9
00:36:51,428 --> 00:36:57,428
Dr. Timothy Reed, played by Brandon Auret.

10
00:40:57,142 --> 00:41:03,142
Midwife, played by Dorothy Ann Gould.

11
00:45:02,857 --> 00:45:08,857
Young Chloe, played by Shayla-Rae McFarlane.

12
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
The Lullaby (also known as Siembamba) is a 2017 South African horror film directed by
Darrell Roodt and co-produced by Samuel Frauenstein and Andre Frauenstein Snr.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
The film stars Reine Swart with Thandi Puren, Brandon Auret, Deànré
Reiners, and Dorothy Ann Gould in supporting roles.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
The film tells the story of 19-year-old mom, Chloe van Heerden, who struggled to dealing with her super
critical mother, Ruby, where she finally ends in a paranoia that sends Chloe into a dark depression.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
This is the first purely South African film production
to release theatrically in the USA.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
Rotten Tomatoes ranked the film as the 17th Best Horror Movie for 2018.

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
The film was shot in and around Pretoria, Gauteng, South Africa.

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
It premiered at the 2017 South African Horrorfest Film Festival.

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of mother, baby, single mother, postpartum depression.

20
01:21:54,285 --> 01:22:00,285
The tone is dark.
